      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry yes the comment isn\u0027t clear, I\u0027ll update - by header I mean the \u0027NV_INDEX\u0027 data.\n\nSimilar to above:\n\nI guess it doesn\u0027t *have* to, but it always is (and it wouldn\u0027t make much sense for it to not be) - so I wanted to avoid implementing partial reads as they would not be used, and if they are, then it means the TPM NVRAM implementation has changed, and we should probably be revisiting all of this rather than just allowing partial reads and hoping for the best..\n\nWDYT?",
